cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pycomorb in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "pycomorb: Time-aware comorbidity and frailty scores from ICD codes"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Fassbender
    given-names: "Finn S."
    email: research@finnfassbender.de
    affiliation: "Institute of Medical Informatics, Charité - Universitätsmedizin Berlin"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-1135-853X"
repository-code: "https://github.com/CUB-CORR/pycomorb"
url: "https://github.com/CUB-CORR/pycomorb"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Python package that computes comorbidity and frailty scores from ICD-9 and
  ICD-10 diagnosis codes using polars: Charlson (many mappings and weights),
  Elixhauser, Combined Comorbidity Score and Hospital Frailty Risk Score.
  Ships the official year-specific ICD-10-GM and ICD-10-CM code-transfer
  tables, so codes recorded in different years are made comparable.
keywords:
